<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polisario Front</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1973">1973</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Frente Polisario</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polisario Front is a Sahrawi nationalist movement founded in May 1973 to end Spanish rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-sahara">Western Sahara</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> handed the territory to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a>, it proclaimed the Sahrawi Arab Democratic Republic in February 1976 and fought both countries, forcing Mauritania to withdraw in 1979. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> ceasefire with Morocco in 1991 promised a referendum that never took place, and fighting resumed in 2020.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polisario-front.jpg" alt="Polisario Front" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: El Uali Mustafá Sayed from Polisario Front · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Sahrawi_Arab_Democratic_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
